From: C2000MAX maintainers <noreply@example.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 20:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: mediatek: apply HQoS to external uplinks

C2000MAX uses an HNAT external device such as eth2 for its cellular
uplink while the ordinary HNAT WAN endpoint is intentionally empty in LAN
role.  HQOS_FLAG only recognized an Ethernet WAN output, so LAN-to-cellular
FOE entries kept their QID but were committed with fqos and QDMA tport
disabled.  The configured upload queue consequently never shaped the
hardware fast path.

Treat an external output as an HQoS uplink only when the packet originated
from a LAN, WED, or virtual ingress.  This covers wired and Wi-Fi clients
without changing external-to-LAN downlink handling or external-to-external
flows.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat.h | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat.h
@@ -1476,8 +1476,13 @@ enum FoeIpAct {
 #define PINGPONG_EXT_ID GENMASK(5, 0)
 #define PINGPONG_MAPE_TOKEN 0x01
 
+#define IS_HQOS_EXT_UL_PATH(dev, skb)\
+	(IS_EXT(dev) && (FROM_GE_LAN_GRP(skb) || FROM_WED(skb) ||\
+			 FROM_GE_VIRTUAL(skb)))
+
 #define HQOS_FLAG(dev, skb, qid)				\
-	((IS_HQOS_UL_MODE && IS_WAN(dev)) ||			\
+	((IS_HQOS_UL_MODE && (IS_WAN(dev) ||			\
+			      IS_HQOS_EXT_UL_PATH(dev, skb))) ||	\
 	 (IS_HQOS_DL_MODE && IS_LAN_GRP(dev)) ||		\
 	 (IS_PPPQ_MODE && (IS_PPPQ_PATH(dev, skb) ||		\
 			   qid >= MAX_PPPQ_QUEUE_NUM)))
